# The Docker build context is the repository root (see Dockerfile), so this file
# decides what reaches the daemon. It is a size and safety boundary, not a
# substitute for .gitignore: `.dockerignore` also has to exclude things that ARE
# tracked in git, such as .env.example and .github/.

# ── Version control and CI ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Nothing here is an input to the image. In particular .github/ carries the
# workflow that builds this image: leaving it in context would let the build
# consume the definition of itself.
.git
.gitignore
.github
.gitattributes
.kilo

# ── Dependencies ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Recreated inside the image by `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile`. Copying the
# host's node_modules in would also copy the host's platform and would defeat
# the lockfile.
node_modules
**/node_modules
.pnpm-store
**/.pnpm-store

# ── Build output ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Stale local `dist/` directories would shadow the fresh build (nest-cli.json
# sets deleteOutDir, but only for apps/api) and would be baked into the image
# if the build failed partway.
dist
**/dist
build
**/build
*.tsbuildinfo

# ── Test artifacts ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
coverage
**/coverage
.nyc_output
**/.nyc_output
test-ledger
**/test-ledger

# ── Solana build output ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ~1.4 GB of Rust target/. anchor build is a separate CI job; the API image
# talks to Solana over RPC and has no reason to carry a compiler.
programs/braice-governance/target
programs/braice-governance/.anchor
programs/braice-governance/tests

# ── Secrets and local configuration ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Every file matching .env* is excluded, including .env.example. This is the
# single most important rule here: apps/api resolves its config from
# `../../../../.env` at boot, so a .env copied into a layer would be read by
# the container and would survive in the image forever, readable by anyone who
# can pull it.
.env
**/.env
.env.*
**/.env.*
*.pem
**/*.pem
*.key
**/*.key
# Solana wallet material. `keypair.json` is what solana-keygen writes and
# SOLANA_KEYPAIR_PATH points at one; it must never enter a layer.
**/id.json
**/*-keypair.json

# ── Editor, OS and log noise ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode
.idea
**/*.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db